  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 200 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nWednesday through Monday:\n\nWhile the previous days cold front slides south into IL/IN \nregion, expect it to stall across that area for Wednesday. \nMeanwhile, models prog high pressure to build across the Great \nLakes for midweek. However, depending on how far south each of \nthese features sets up will determine our rain chances through \nthe second half of the week. Continue to see the GFS/GEFS trend \ntoward a more southward extent of this high pressure thus \nlimiting the shower/storm activity along the low-level WAA and \nahead of the stalled front to our south. Meanwhile the ECMWF/EPS\nis more in favor of the low-level WAA and associated \nshowers/storms to trend far enough northward to overcome the \nsubsidence from the surface high and has been more of an \ninfluence on the NBM PoP chances. Ultimately, will depend on \nplacement, but for now will continue to maintain some PoP \nmentions especially for far southern portions of the CWA \nWednesday and Thursday.\n\nOtherwise, expect a taste of fall for the second half of the \nweek and upper-level zonal flow dominates the the pattern with \ndaily highs in the 60s/70s and overnight lows in the 50s to \naround 60F.\n\nToward the end of the week expect the pattern to shift as long \nrange models prog trough to develop over the Pacific Northwest \nduring the day Friday and drift across the central CONUS through\nthe weekend. As this systems develops and traverses into our \nneck of the woods, expect to see a more active trend heading \ninto the weekend. Continue to see a signal for a weak surface \nlow to develop over the Plains and lift across the Great Lake \nlater Friday into Saturday. Will see periodic rain chances \nassociated with this system as the low-level WAA and warm front \nahead of it could bring a round of showers and storms along with\na bit milder temps. Then as the low passes through WI, it will \nlikely bring additional chances through the weekend, but exact \ntiming and amounts remains uncertain given model and timing \ndifference this far out. \n\nWagner",
